 "caveats": [
  "Weights are the artifact's calibrated weights and are not recalibrated; the UK calibration surface now carries a UC caseload target (microcosm#735), which would absorb part of any move in a real build.",
  "OLD and NEW are the same microcosm machinery at the same seed, so NEW-OLD isolates the arithmetic split; OLD is not the incumbent's own draw (microimpute 10-point quantile grid vs RegimeGatedQRF continuous quantile over the full leaf conditional) - the OLD re-draw sits 1.15m benefit units below the incumbent artifact on the same households, a draw-machinery/predictor-surface difference outside this change.",
  "The recipient predictor surface is materialised from the released h5 (num_bedrooms is absent there, so the engine default 0 is used; incomes are the post-SPI h5 incomes), not from the FRS spine the build runs on.",
  "SPI-synthetic clone households are re-imputed like any household.",
